</div>',
  '<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Client Profiles to Target</div>
<p><strong>DIY investors holding concentrated Canadian energy:</strong> Self-directed investors who added energy exposure during the Hormuz rally and have not rebalanced. They have no framework for the resolution tail risk and no one to run the scenario analysis with them.</p>
<p><strong>Investors with international equity exposure watching energy underperformance:</strong> Clients or prospects who hold global mandates without TSX energy and have watched Canadian energy outperform in 2026. The FOMO conversation is a prospecting window, because the entry point they''re considering is also the point of maximum resolution risk.</p>
<p><strong>Energy sector employees or executives:</strong> Clients whose human capital is already correlated with oil prices and who may be adding financial capital exposure on top of that concentration. The conversation about diversifying correlated risk is most persuasive in a high-price environment, not after the correction.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Opening Line</div>
<div class="script-box">Iran and Israel exchanged strikes over the weekend, oil spiked and then came back, and the Strait of Hormuz is still closed this morning. I''m calling because the energy trade that has driven most of the TSX''s performance in 2026 is at a point where the risk profile has shifted, and I wanted to make sure you had the full picture before making any decisions about your exposure.</div>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Value Proposition</div>
<p>The geopolitical risk embedded in energy prices right now is not a market insight. It is in every headline. The insight that is not in every headline is that the same positions which have performed brilliantly during the Hormuz closure period carry a specific and rapid downside risk in a resolution scenario that most investors are not modelling. The advisor who brings the scenario analysis, the portfolio weight audit, and the rebalancing framework is delivering a service the energy news cannot.</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Discovery Questions</div>
<p>What percentage of your portfolio do you think is currently in Canadian energy?</p>
<p>When did you last rebalance your energy holdings relative to your target allocation?</p>
<p>If WTI dropped to $65 on a diplomatic resolution, what would that do to your portfolio and how would you feel about it?</p>
<p>Is anyone running scenario analysis for you on the geopolitical risk in your energy positions?</p>
</div>
<div class="toolkit-section">
<div class="toolkit-section-label">Prospecting Email Template</div>
